{"name":"Sea Bed","hex":"#29848d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea bed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of seabed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_bed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seabed","blocks":[{"text":"The seabed is the bottom of the ocean. Alternatively, it is known as the seafloor, sea floor, ocean floor, or ocean bottom. The floor of all the world's oceans is known as the seabed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Common_stingray_tenerife.jpg/330px-Common_stingray_tenerife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seabed"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"},{"title":"Bed","blocks":[{"text":"A bed is a piece of furniture that is used as a place to sleep, rest, and relax."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg/330px-2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif/500px-Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Mid